  `r` with shape `[I, J, ..., L, num_rows, num_cols]`.

  The second innermost dimension of `diagonal` has double meaning.
  When `k` is scalar or `k[0] == k[1]`, `M` is part of the batch size
  [I, J, ..., M], and the output tensor is:

  ```
  output[i, j, ..., l, m, n]
